module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Curves.VanishingResults.DualizingFirstCohomologyDimension
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Curves.VanishingResults.DualizingSheafClauseFive
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Curves.VanishingResults.GlobalSectionsGeneration
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Global generation near a zero-dimensional quotient of an extension of `ω_X`

In Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B5D] — a field `k` and a proper one-dimensional `k`-scheme `X` with
`H⁰(X, 𝒪_X) = k` — let `ω_X = H^{-1}(f^×(𝒪_{Spec k}))` be the dualizing sheaf of
[Stacks, Tag 0BS2]. This file states [Stacks, Tag 0B5F] for that sheaf.

`AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.epi_globalSectionsHom_comp` proves the lemma for
any quasi-coherent `ω` satisfying clause (5) of [Stacks, Tag 0BS2] and `dim_k H¹(X, ω) = 1`.
Both properties hold for the dualizing sheaf, with nothing carried (names in the namespace
`AlgebraicGeometry.CohenMacaulayCurveSituation` unless qualified):

* clause (5) is `firstCohomologyDuality_dualizingSheafOverField`,
* `dim_k H¹(X, ω_X) = 1` is `finrank_cohomologyOverField_one_dualizingSheafOverField_eq_one`,
* quasi-coherence of `ω_X` is `Stacks.Duality.isQuasicoherent_dualizingSheafOverField`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B5F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B5F)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

namespace CohenMacaulayCurveSituation

variable {S : CohenMacaulayCurveSituation.{u}}

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0B5F.** In Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B5D], let
`ω_X = H^{-1}(f^×(𝒪_{Spec k}))` be the dualizing sheaf of `X` ([Stacks, Tag 0BS2]) and let
`ω_X ⟶ ℱ ⟶ 𝒬 ⟶ 0` be an exact sequence of coherent `𝒪_X`-modules such that the support of `𝒬`
has dimension at most zero, `dim_k H⁰(X, 𝒬) ≥ 2`, and no nonzero submodule of `ℱ` maps
injectively to `𝒬`. Then the submodule of `ℱ` generated by the global sections of `ℱ` surjects
onto `𝒬`, i.e. the composite of `AlgebraicGeometry.globalSectionsHom ℱ` with `ℱ ⟶ 𝒬` is an
epimorphism.

Coherence of `ℱ` enters as quasi-coherence and finite type; of `𝒬` only quasi-coherence is used.
This is `epi_globalSectionsHom_comp` at the dualizing sheaf, whose two properties are proved. -/
@[stacks 0B5F]
public theorem epi_globalSectionsHom_comp_dualizingSheafOverField {F Q : S.X.Modules}
    (hFq : F.IsQuasicoherent) (hFft : F.IsFiniteType) (hQq : Q.IsQuasicoherent)
    (α : Stacks.Duality.dualizingSheafOverField S.f ⟶ F) (β : F ⟶ Q) (hαβ : α ≫ β = 0)
    (hex : (ShortComplex.mk α β hαβ).Exact) [Epi β]
    (hQdim : topologicalKrullDim (SheafOfModules.supp Q) ≤ 0)
    (htwo : 2 ≤ Module.finrank S.k (cohomologyOverField S.k S.f Q 0))
    (hnosub : ∀ (M : S.X.Modules) (u : M ⟶ F), Mono u → Mono (u ≫ β) → IsZero M) :
    Epi (globalSectionsHom F ≫ β) :=
  epi_globalSectionsHom_comp (Stacks.Duality.isQuasicoherent_dualizingSheafOverField S.f)
    hFq hFft hQq (firstCohomologyDuality_dualizingSheafOverField S)
    (finrank_cohomologyOverField_one_dualizingSheafOverField_eq_one S) α β hαβ hex hQdim htwo
    hnosub

end CohenMacaulayCurveSituation

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
